**Reject unresolvable nested ids instead of stringifying the object.**

When `id` is an object that `normalizeRecordId` cannot resolve, `String(id)` produces `"[object Object]"`. The function then returns an id such as `"objective:[object Object]"`. `convertLegacyResourceRecord` accepts it because the value is a string, so a corrupt record id enters the DataFn import payload and can collide with other unresolvable records from the same table.

<details>
<summary>🐛 Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
-  if (typeof table === "string" && id !== undefined && id !== null) {
-    return `${table}:${normalizeRecordId(id) ?? String(id)}`;
-  }
+  if (typeof table === "string" && id !== undefined && id !== null) {
+    const nested = normalizeRecordId(id);
+    return nested ? `${table}:${nested}` : undefined;
+  }
```
</details>

