P2: Removing this `<span id="global-sync-status">` orphans a live consumer: `SyncStatusListener.refreshFromGlobal()` calls `document.getElementById("global-sync-status")?.getAttribute("data-syncstatus")` so it can pick up an in-progress sync on mount, and the span was the only place that element was ever created. After this removal the lookup always returns undefined, so `refreshFromGlobal` silently becomes a no-op and a newly mounted sync listener no longer reflects the current global sync status on initial load. Update `SyncStatusListener.refreshFromGlobal` (or remove it) to stop reading the deleted element, and confirm the span isn't needed for initial sync feedback.

