On browsers or embedded WebViews that implement IndexedDB but not `indexedDB.databases()`, this returns `undefined`, causing `detectLegacyLocalData()` to report `isSupported: false`; `UserBaseLayer` then skips the recovery gate and starts with an empty DataFn database even though the active user's legacy `${userId}-1` or `${dapId}-1` database is still present. Probe the deterministic legacy database names when enumeration is unavailable so existing local-only users do not lose access to their data after upgrading.

