**Handle `initializeLegacyFlux` failures in the startup path.**

`initializeLegacyFlux` throws when `getDapId()` returns a falsy value (Line 204) and it propagates any `initFlux` rejection. `initializeDatabase` catches its own failures and sets `error`, but this step does not. `onMount` calls `startApplication()` at Line 153 without a `try`/`catch`, so the rejection is unhandled, `error` stays `null`, and `$appLoadingState.isBaseLoaded` is never set. The template then keeps `AppLoadingView` with an empty message, and the user cannot reach the app or see `PageError`.

