If writing the disabled metadata or `cloneUpAllDatafnData()` fails, this has already removed E2EE from the live client. The catch restores the old metadata and calls `initializeNucleumDatafn()`, but the runtime key still contains the same `keyRef`, so initialization returns the existing runtime without reinstalling its provider. Subsequent sync writes can therefore remain unencrypted even though both local and remote settings still report E2EE enabled; explicitly restore the provider/context before propagating the failure.

